[debug] [2026-09-23T14:01:16.260Z] Command:       /usr/bin/node /home/abdullah/.npm-global/bin/firebase appdistribution:distribute ant_app/build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk --app 1:514133180208:android:45009c17a5721198b2d2f5 --project ant-assistive-nav --groups fydp --release-notes Round 4 — the model can reach all its tools again.

Fixes from the 22 and 23 September field reports:

- Routing works for Bangla place names again. "ধানমন্ডি ল্যাব এইড" was being
  cut to "ধানমন্ডি ল্" before it ever reached the geocoder.
- "Nearest bathroom / restaurant / pharmacy" now routes. It used to be sent
  to a search that only answers "where is this name".
- Scene questions reach the camera. "What colour is that", "what does this
  say" — the tool was not being offered at all, which is why it answered
  that it was a navigation assistant.
- "What's in front of me" takes one frame, not a 17-second three-frame sweep.
- The camera now says Left / Straight ahead / Right during a sweep, with one
  buzz for left and two for right. The narration existed and was never wired.
- Drop-off detection works. The depth model had been returning an empty
  buffer on every scan since it was added.
- Signs and close-up detail upload at 640x480 instead of 320x240.
- Pressing the mic stops the assistant mid-sentence instead of reading out
  the whole backlog.
- It no longer reads markdown symbols aloud.
- Turning off "Hey ANT" in Bangla works. The spelling people actually say
  was missing from the list.
- An emergency contact can no longer be saved with a phone number you did
  not give — it asks.
- Text size has five named steps instead of a continuous slider.

New:
- A guardian's snapshot request is answered with the photo and a description.
  It used to reply that the ability would be added later.
- The frame a scan answered from is shown in the chat.
- Weather warnings before setting off — rain, storms, heat.
- Bus stops and crossings are announced as you approach them.
- Caretaker voice messages can be replayed: "play that again", "the one
  before that".
- Low battery is announced when path-watching stops.

Chat now answers on Gemini first, Groq second. Groq is faster but its free
tier ran out mid-session last time and locked out for 25 minutes at a stretch.
